.Dd August 31, 2026
.Dt FILEES-ADMIN 8
.Os
.Sh NAME
.Nm filees-admin
.Nd FileES administrative tickets, revocation, repository repair and erasure closure
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.Nm
.Op Fl config Ar path
.Cm ticket create Ar mailbox
.Op Fl -ttl Ar duration
.Op Fl -join-realm-alias Ar alias
.Nm
.Op Fl config Ar path
.Cm ticket resend Fl -ticket-id Ar uuid
.Nm
.Op Fl config Ar path
.Cm ticket revoke Fl -ticket-id Ar uuid
.Nm
.Op Fl config Ar path
.Cm ticket list
.Nm
.Op Fl config Ar path
.Cm operation inspect Fl -operation-id Ar uuid
.Nm
.Op Fl config Ar path
.Cm client revoke Fl -client-id Ar uuid
.Op Fl -reason Ar text
.Nm
.Op Fl config Ar path
.Cm client revoke-realm Fl -realm-id Ar uuid
.Op Fl -reason Ar text
.Nm
.Op Fl config Ar path
.Cm repo transfer-owner Fl -repo-id Ar uuid Fl -realm-id Ar uuid
.Nm
.Op Fl config Ar path
.Cm repo check-state
.Op Fl -realm-id Ar uuid
.Nm
.Op Fl config Ar path
.Cm repo prune
.Op Fl -realm-id Ar uuid
.Op Fl -older-than Ar duration
.Op Fl -apply
.Nm
.Op Fl config Ar path
.Cm erasure complete Fl -operation-id Ar uuid
.Op Fl -partially-retained
.Nm
.Cm version
.Sh DESCRIPTION
.Nm
is the operator command for onboarding tickets and a small set of
fail-closed administrative actions.
It writes structured JSON to standard output and diagnostics to standard
error.
It must run with effective user
.Sy _filees-state .
Creating a ticket as root produces a root-owned mode 0600 file that the
set-id onboarding entry intentionally cannot read.
.Pp
.Cm version
is answered before the configuration is opened, so a stale binary can be
identified even when
.Pa server.json
is suspect.
.Pp
Normal repository create, grants, public shares and realm removal are desktop
control-plane operations.
The
.Cm repo check-state
and
.Cm repo prune
verbs are exceptional operator recovery tools for abandoned repository
creation state, not an alternate repository-management interface.
.Sh COMMANDS
.Bl -tag -width Ds
.It Cm ticket create
Issue a one-time invitation to
.Ar mailbox
and send it immediately.
The mailbox must come before any flag.
Without
.Fl -join-realm-alias
the ticket authorises a new realm.
With the flag the server resolves the immutable alias now and stores the
approved realm ID; the client never submits that ID.
The invitation capability is not printed.
.It Cm ticket resend
Replace a failed delivery capability without changing recipient or TTL.
.It Cm ticket revoke
Delete an unused ticket.
A claimed ticket has already been replaced by an operation bundle.
.It Cm ticket list
List remaining tickets.
Names are
.Fn sha256 mailbox
so the file name does not reveal the address.
.It Cm operation inspect
Show one onboarding operation.
.It Cm client revoke
Write a durable
.Cm revoking
record, drop generated SSH/SVN access, then commit the revoked client.
An identical retry is idempotent; a different reason is rejected.
.It Cm client revoke-realm
Revoke every installation of a realm with the same sequence.
.It Cm repo transfer-owner
Change
.Ic owner_realm_id
and regenerate data-authz.
Existing grants issued by the previous owner are not touched.
.It Cm repo check-state
Read repository-creation backend records and correlate them with canonical
authority, FSFS/staging presence and, for a possible abandoned initial
creation,
.Xr svnlook 1
youngest revision.
Normal active repositories are omitted.
The optional
.Fl -realm-id
limits the JSON report to one realm.
This command does not remove repositories.
.It Cm repo prune
Report the same abandoned-creation candidates as
.Cm repo check-state .
Without
.Fl -apply
it is a dry run and changes nothing.
.Fl -older-than
defaults to 1h and prevents a recent creation attempt from being selected.
With
.Fl -apply ,
only records marked
.Ic prunable
and old enough are removed.
For a published candidate the canonical state must be
.Ic initializing ,
there must be no staging tree, and FSFS must be absent or exactly r0.
Before removal the command durably records
.Ic prune_pending ,
blocks commits and checks the youngest revision again.
An active repository, an initializing repository at r1 or later, and an
ordinary deletion tombstone are never removed by this path.
.It Cm erasure complete
Close a data-erasure request after the operator has verified backup
retention.
.Fl -partially-retained
records that policy still requires some copies.
.El
.Sh EXIT STATUS
.Nm
uses
.Xr sysexits 3
values:
.Bl -tag -width 4n -compact
.It 0
success
.It 64
bad arguments
.It 65
input data error
.It 69
resource unavailable
.It 70
internal error
.It 75
temporary failure
.It 78
configuration error
.El
.Sh EXAMPLES
Create a new-realm invitation:
.Bd -literal -offset indent
$ doas -u _filees-state filees-admin ticket create user@example.com
.Ed
.Pp
Authorise another desktop in an existing realm:
.Bd -literal -offset indent
$ doas -u _filees-state filees-admin ticket create user@example.com \e
    --join-realm-alias acme --ttl 24h
.Ed
.Pp
Inspect and then remove abandoned empty initial creations for one realm:
.Bd -literal -offset indent
$ doas -u _filees-state filees-admin repo check-state --realm-id UUID
$ doas -u _filees-state filees-admin repo prune --realm-id UUID \e
    --older-than 1h
$ doas -u _filees-state filees-admin repo prune --realm-id UUID \e
    --older-than 1h --apply
.Ed
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr filees 7 ,
.Xr filees.conf 5 ,
.Xr filees-operation 8 ,
.Xr filees-mail 8
